{
  "requirement": "The `habeas-requirements` skill MUST direct agents to show the edits a review made to requirements outside its group in the same way as {cite}`requirements.cli.requirements_review_skill.present.mechanical` requires. It MUST also direct them to list every `{example}` a review added and to say that each one needs a test.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "structural: `requirements.cli.requirements_review_skill.present.outside` has no structural obligation. It names no library, algorithm, signature, type, field, or delegation through a named interface. It only says what the `habeas-requirements` skill MUST direct agents to do. That is a requirement on the skill's content: (a) show edits made outside a group in the manner `requirements.cli.requirements_review_skill.present.mechanical` requires, and (b) list every added `{example}` and say each needs a test. A skill document that says the same thing in other words, or in a different place, would satisfy it, so the form is discretionary.\n\nThe review root `assets/skills/habeas-requirements/SKILL.md` does carry this direction. In `section[Habeas requirements]/section[Workflow]`, step 4 (`paragraph@7b764a629ec4`) says: \"Show text that was already agreed or that the user supplied as a diff against that text, then a 'Mechanical:' list of the changes. Show the edits reviewers made outside their group the same way, and list added `{example}`s, which each need a test. Don't raise mechanical changes to new text as questions.\" That matches both clauses, and it reproduces the mechanical presentation rule that the cited requirement sets. No further implementation root or marker is needed.\n\nbehavioral: The subject has two behavioral obligations, and both are content directions in the bundled `habeas-requirements` skill. First, the skill must direct agents to show edits made outside the group in the same way as `requirements.cli.requirements_review_skill.present.mechanical` requires (a diff plus a mechanical-changes list). Second, it must direct agents to list every `{example}` a review added and say each needs a test.\n\nThe only test is `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[the_requirements_skill_shows_edits_outside_a_group_and_added_examples]`. It is marked `{test}` for the subject. It calls `assert_in_order` on `habeas-requirements`, which reads the bundled skill through `bundled_skill`. `bundled_skill` collapses whitespace, so line wraps in `SKILL.md` do not matter. `assert_text_in_order` requires each phrase to appear after the previous one and panics if one is missing.\n\nThe test asserts two phrases:\n- It asserts `as a diff against that text, then a \"Mechanical:\" list`. This anchors the convention that \"the same way\" refers to.\n- It then asserts `Show the edits reviewers made outside their group the same way, and list added `{example}`s, which each need a test`. This covers the edits-outside-the-group direction, listing added examples, and the need for a test on each.\n\nI read the workflow step 4 paragraph in `assets/skills/habeas-requirements/SKILL.md`. It contains both phrases, in that order. Removing or rewording any of the three directives would make the test fail. Placing the outside-group direction before the convention it refers to would fail it too.\n\nThe skill's direction not to raise mechanical changes to new text as questions belongs to the cited requirement `present.mechanical`. It is not assessed here. The subject imposes no other obligations, and no gaps are acknowledged.",
  "references": "fb6848e8816ff947f001b14f4000a7afa622f7b517701f6dfc3c9983d7c7661b",
