      "output": {
        "status": "success",
        "rationale": "The subject has two behavioral obligations, and both are content directions in the bundled `habeas-requirements` skill. First, the skill must direct agents to show edits made outside the group in the same way as `requirements.cli.requirements_review_skill.present.mechanical` requires (a diff plus a mechanical-changes list). Second, it must direct agents to list every `{example}` a review added and say each needs a test.\n\nThe only test is `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[the_requirements_skill_shows_edits_outside_a_group_and_added_examples]`. It is marked `{test}` for the subject. It calls `assert_in_order` on `habeas-requirements`, which reads the bundled skill through `bundled_skill`. `bundled_skill` collapses whitespace, so line wraps in `SKILL.md` do not matter. `assert_text_in_order` requires each phrase to appear after the previous one and panics if one is missing.\n\nThe test asserts two phrases:\n- It asserts `as a diff against that text, then a \"Mechanical:\" list`. This anchors the convention that \"the same way\" refers to.\n- It then asserts `Show the edits reviewers made outside their group the same way, and list added `{example}`s, which each need a test`. This covers the edits-outside-the-group direction, listing added examples, and the need for a test on each.\n\nI read the workflow step 4 paragraph in `assets/skills/habeas-requirements/SKILL.md`. It contains both phrases, in that order. Removing or rewording any of the three directives would make the test fail. Placing the outside-group direction before the convention it refers to would fail it too.\n\nThe skill's direction not to raise mechanical changes to new text as questions belongs to the cited requirement `present.mechanical`. It is not assessed here. The subject imposes no other obligations, and no gaps are acknowledged."
      }
